  "notes": "Cross-client canonical vectors for schema-migration body v1: migration identity, language-neutral structured operation args (DTO serde field names with exact values, exact source bytes and bit-exact rule bounds including negative zero; absent args mean the DTO default), per-operation prose descriptions, and expected canonical bytes plus SHA-256 checksums. Bytes were derived independently from the grammar documented in shamir-query-types canonical/body.rs, canonical/ddl.rs, canonical/function.rs and security/hmac.rs; the first case reproduces the committed golden vector of test-vectors/schema_migration_v1.json byte for byte. The TypeScript step consumes this same file; the Rust test rebuilds every case from the typed DDL builders and rejects drift by asserting both the operation variant sequence and every structured arg against the built operations."
}
